    LLM: 'Game: Kani (Gonin-Kan). Type: Hidden Partnership Trick-taking. Deck: 50 cards. Hand: 10 cards. Partnership: Joker holder + Ace of trumps = Kankei. Trumps rotate: â™£â†’â™¦â†’â™¥â†’â™ . Joker: strongest but banned from first/last trick. Scoring: A-K-Q-J = 1pt each (16 total). Kankei wins with 9+ points. Play: Counter-clockwise, must follow suit.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Kani! You have 10 cards. The trumps rotate each round. Watch for the Joker and the Ace of trumpsâ€”those players are secret partners! Can you figure out who to trust?',
    objective: "Capture 'Point Cards' (A, K, Q, J of each suit). There are 16 points total in the deck.",
    gameplay: "1. **Partnership**: The player with the **Joker** and the player with the **Ace of Trumps** form the 'Kankei' team. The other three players are the 'Mukankei' team. 2. **The Joker**: The Joker is the strongest card but cannot be played to the first or last trick of a round. 3. **Play**: Counter-clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.",
